@* Decision 0011 (run W2, WU4): the toast area. shell.js showToast({ title, body, tone }) clones #toast-template into #toasts; tone is "ok",
   "warn", "danger" or "info" (the status dot's colour). A page may also render toasts here itself with the same markup. *@
<div class="toast-container position-fixed bottom-0 end-0 p-3" id="toasts" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="false"></div>
<template id="toast-template">
  <div class="toast" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
    <div class="toast-header">
      <span class="status-dot ok me-2" data-toast-dot></span>
      <strong class="me-auto" data-toast-title></strong>
      <small>now</small>
      <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="toast" aria-label="Close"></button>
    </div>
    <div class="toast-body" data-toast-body></div>
  </div>
</template>
